<node id="Multi-Head Attention Mechanism (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Head Attention Mechanism (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation defines the Multi-Head Attention mechanism in Transformer models, enabling the model to jointly attend to information from different representation subspaces, enhancing its ability to process sequences effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a1ff7410a8c7b47965680cc9fe84eb9</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763838602</data>
</node>
<node id="Feed-Forward Neural Network (FFN) Layer (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Feed-Forward Neural Network (FFN) Layer (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">The FFN equation defines a layer in neural networks that applies linear transformations followed by a non-linear activation function, enabling the model to learn complex patterns in data. It plays a crucial role in the Transformer architecture, enhancing its ability to process sequences effectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df83cfb06d7ca1e9f3c6dd49bea88aed</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763838602</data>
</node>
