<node id="Comparative Analysis of Layer Types in Sequence Models (table)">
  <data key="d0">Comparative Analysis of Layer Types in Sequence Models (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">This table compares the computational complexity, sequential operations, and maximum path lengths of self-attention, recurrent, and convolutional layers, highlighting the efficiency of self-attention in handling long-range dependencies in sequence transduction tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fccc14c59791ca485ddcc6c46f262b0c</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763838602</data>
